1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,952
Same 100 million won in Starbucks stock: one lost 20 million, one made 30 million

2
00:00:05,972 --> 00:00:13,755
Bought near the July 2021 peak: 80 million. Bought Aug 12, 2024: 130 million

3
00:00:13,775 --> 00:00:21,180
Oct 26 close, price only. And the next round is decided at the Oct 29 earnings

4
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:26,256
Aug 12 was the day before Brian Niccol was named CEO

5
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:33,426
On the news the stock rose 24% intraday. Hope moved before results

6
00:00:33,446 --> 00:00:39,915
Niccol would commute 1,600+ km from his California home by company jet

7
00:00:39,935 --> 00:00:45,826
Two subway stops feel far to me; his commute earns miles

8
00:00:45,846 --> 00:00:57,263
He spent on staff and stores first: $7.90 kept per $100 in FY2025; this year's goal is $11+

9
00:00:57,283 --> 00:01:01,936
You can't pick the day you buy, but there are just three numbers to watch

10
00:01:01,956 --> 00:01:10,729
One: U.S. comparable-store sales, the company targets 6.5%+ this quarter

11
00:01:10,749 --> 00:01:16,468
Two: transactions, above last quarter's 4.2% means customers keep growing

12
00:01:16,488 --> 00:01:24,474
Three: profit per $100 sold. Above last year's $7.90 means store spending is paying back

13
00:01:24,494 --> 00:01:30,589
Like and subscribe for more. Full video: profile link
